# SPAXEL firmware anti-rollback security version.
#
# This number is stamped into every firmware image as
# CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_APP_SECURE_VERSION and is what the ESP32-S3 bootloader
# compares against the SECURE_VERSION eFuse field. It is NOT the app version
# (that is ../VERSION) and must not follow it: it moves only when a release
# changes the security posture of the firmware.
#
# Rules (enforced by firmware/scripts/bump-secure-version.sh, see
# docs/notes/anti-rollback-secure-version.md):
#   - integer, >= 0, and only ever increased — never decreased
#   - every increase needs a reason, recorded in firmware/SECURE_VERSION_LOG.md
#   - a node burns its SECURE_VERSION eFuse to match the first image it
#     accepts, and that burn is one-way: a higher eFuse permanently rejects
#     every lower image
#
# Bump with:  ./scripts/bump-secure-version.sh --reason "why"
1
